                                ['type' => 'explanation', 'title' => 'Tense backshift rules', 'body' => "When the reporting verb is past (said, told, explained, asked), shift tenses **one step back**:\n\n| Direct | Reported |\n|--------|----------|\n| Present simple | Past simple |\n| Present continuous | Past continuous |\n| Present perfect | Past perfect |\n| Past simple | Past perfect |\n| Will | Would |\n| Can | Could |\n| Must | Had to / Must |\n\n**Time markers also shift:**\n- today → that day\n- yesterday → the day before\n- tomorrow → the next day\n- this week → that week\n- now → then\n\n**No backshift needed if the reporting verb is present or if the statement is still true:**\n- ✓ \"The Earth is round,\" the teacher says. → The teacher says (that) the Earth is round.\n- ✗ The teacher said that the Earth is round. ✓ (But acceptable when reporting in past context)", 'body_id' => 'Dalam reported speech, waktu mundur satu langkah. Penanda waktu juga berubah: today menjadi that day.'],
